  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When having the selfie stick active, I see a lot of people grab it controller facing downward. Which is the natural way of grabbing because of the handle, However with how grabbing actually works in VRC it gets people frustrated, as you end up pointing the controller nearly a full 90 degrees away from the cameras pickup hit box. \n\nI suggest angling the handle ~45 degrees downward so that when people go to grab it, their controller is on a collision course straight to grabbing the camera like it needs to be grabbed. And hopefully people can also put 2 and 2 together in how their controller interacts with pick ups by seeing that dotted line overlay shows up when you successfully can grab the camera.",
